---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { getLocale, translate } from '../lib/i18n';
const locale = getLocale(Astro.url.pathname);
const t = (message: string) => translate(message, locale);
---
<Shell title={t("Privacy and local data")} description={t("How Peptide Tools handles browser-local protocols, backups, hosting requests and opt-in Google Analytics usage measurement.")}>
  <article class="prose"><div class="page-heading"><h1>{t("Your inputs stay in your browser.")}</h1><p>{t("Updated November 13, 2026.")}</p></div>
    <h2>{t("Calculations and protocols")}</h2><p>{t("Calculation inputs are processed in the page. Saved protocols use this browser’s localStorage. We do not operate an account system, protocol database or cloud sync service.")}</p><p>{t("Browser storage is not encrypted by this application. Other people with access to this browser may access saved entries. Browser data removal deletes them. Use JSON backup, restore and clear controls in the planner.")}</p>
    <p>{t('Product names, brands, label quantities, ingredient lists and your label confirmations are saved locally with your schedules. Version 2 JSON backups include both. Earlier version 1 schedule backups remain readable. Restoring a backup replaces saved products and schedules only after your confirmation.')}</p>
    <p>{t('Plans retain a snapshot of the product label used when they were created. Editing or deleting a product does not silently change an existing plan. Product names and entered amounts are not placed in page URLs.')}</p>
    <h2>{t("Files you export")}</h2><p>{t("JSON backups and calendar files contain your protocol inputs. They are generated locally. If you import a calendar file into a cloud calendar, that provider receives its contents. Printing and downloading are under your control.")}</p>
    <h2>{t("Optional usage analytics")}</h2><p>{t("Google Analytics 4 loads only after you choose “Allow analytics”, and only when production measurement is configured. Declining leaves the tools fully usable. You can change the choice using “Analytics preferences” below.")}</p><p>{t("Usage events measure page groups, starting and completing calculations, generating and saving schedules, downloads and print requests. We do not send entered doses, concentrations, item names, protocol names, notes, search text or exported file contents.")}</p><p>{t("Reference detail URLs and titles are replaced with a generic reference group before analytics events are sent. Source parameters use a fixed allowlist, and referring URLs are reduced to their origin. Advertising features and Google Signals are disabled in the integration.")}</p><p>{t("When allowed, GA4 uses first-party analytics cookies to estimate returning browsers and activity over time. This is pseudonymous measurement, not a count of identifiable people. Consent and blocking can reduce measured coverage. Withdrawing consent removes this site’s analytics cookies and reloads the page to stop the tag.")}</p>
    <p>{t('Product events record starting an entry, saving, opening or deleting a record, and restoring a backup. Only the fixed single-ingredient or blend category may be included. Product identifiers, names, brands, label facts and schedule contents are excluded.')}</p>
    <h2>{t("Consent storage and hosting")}</h2><p>{t("Your language preference is stored in this browser. The default language is English.")} {t("Switching language temporarily keeps the open form in sessionStorage on this device; it is removed after restoring the form or expires after one minute.")}</p><p>{t("A localStorage entry stores your analytics preference; sessionStorage avoids repeated start events during a browser-tab session. Hosting via Vercel necessarily processes ordinary network requests, including an IP address and requested URL. Browser-local protocol storage does not eliminate hosting logs.")}</p><p>{t("Google Search Console reports search performance. It does not require a visitor tracking script on this website. External source links open with no referrer information sent by this site.")}</p><p>{t("See")} <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">{t("Google’s privacy policy")}</a> {t("and")} <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">{t("Vercel’s privacy policy")}</a>.</p>
    <p>{t('Choosing to carry a calculation into a plan keeps its product identifier, entered amount and unit in sessionStorage for up to five minutes. The draft is consumed when the planner opens. It is not sent to analytics or a server.')}</p>
  </article>
</Shell>
